    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` computed field following the codebase's existing idioms for derived owner attributes (like `locality`, `fiscalYear`, `ageBand`), keeping each piece of logic in a small single-responsibility unit:\n\n1. **`LocalityResolver.isKnownRegion(String)`** \u2014 added a query answering \"is this a known canonical region?\" (NSW/VIC/QLD), which belongs here alongside the region tables rather than being duplicated elsewhere.\n\n2. **`OwnerSegment`** (new value class in `model`) \u2014 composes the segment `<TIER>_<AREA>`: `PREMIUM` when membership level \u2265 3 else `STANDARD`, and `METRO` when the locality is a known region else `REGIONAL`. It delegates the region check to `LocalityResolver`, mirroring the `AgeBand`/`FiscalYear` helper pattern.\n\n3. **`Owner.getOwnerSegment()`** \u2014 a thin `@Transient` getter delegating to `OwnerSegment.of(getMembershipLevel(), getLocality())`, reusing the existing membership-level and locality logic rather than recomputing anything.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the read-only `ownerSegment` field (with the four-value enum) on the owner schema, so MapStruct auto-maps the getter into the response DTO by name, consistent with the sibling computed fields.\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known region, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown one) pass.",
